owski</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transposable elements as a significant source of transcription regulating signals</article-title><source>Gene</source><year>2006</year><volume>365</volume><fpage>104</fpage><lpage>110</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16376497</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.gene.2005.09.036</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brosius</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>RNAs from all categories generate retrosequences that may be exapted as novel genes or regulatory elements</article-title><source>Gene</source><year>1999</year><volume>238</volume><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>134</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10570990</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0378-1119(99)00227-9</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Britten</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>DNA sequence insertion and evolutionary variation in gene regulation</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>1996</year><volume>93</volume><fpage>9374</fpage><lpage>9377</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8790336</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.93.18.9374</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Britten</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mobile elements inserted in the distant past have taken on important functions</article-title><source>Gene</source><year>1997</year><volume>205</volume><fpage>177</fpage><lpage>182</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9461392</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0378-1119(97)00399-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type=